# q2_inode
Task 2.3  maximum file size for the given inode
block size        : 4096 bytes
pointer size      : 4 bytes
pointers per block: 1024

  direct        12 pointers -> 12 blocks
  single       1024 pointers -> 1024 blocks
  double  1024^2 pointers -> 1048576 blocks
  triple  1024^3 pointers -> 1073741824 blocks
  ------------------------------------------------
  total                  -> 1074791436 blocks
  in bytes               -> 4402345721856 bytes
  in human units         -> 4.004 TiB  (4.402 TB)

reads needed to reach a block
  blocks 0-11            : direct pointer       1 read
  blocks 12-1035         : single indirect      2 reads
  blocks 1036-1049611    : double indirect      3 reads
  blocks above that      : triple indirect      4 reads

how many bytes each level covers
  direct    :    49152 bytes (48.0 KiB)
  single    :  4194304 bytes (4.0 MiB)
  double    : 4294967296 bytes (4096.0 MiB)
  triple    : 4398046511104 bytes (4.000 TiB)

the 4 GB file of the assignment needs 1048576 blocks,
so it is described by the direct pointers plus part of the
single-indirect block: it never touches the double indirect.
